AWS Cost Optimization – Interview Guide
🔹 1. What is AWS Cost Optimization?
Answer:
 Cost optimization is the process of reducing cloud spending while maintaining performance and reliability.
It follows the AWS Well-Architected Framework (Cost Optimization Pillar).
🔹 2. Key Principles of Cost Optimization
Pay only for what you use
Right-size resources
Use managed services
Monitor and optimize continuously
Use pricing models wisely
🔹 3. Core AWS Services for Cost Optimization
📊 Monitoring & Billing
AWS Cost Explorer → Analyze usage and trends
AWS Budgets → Set alerts
Amazon CloudWatch → Track metrics
🔹 4. EC2 Cost Optimization
💡 Best Practices:
Use right instance type (avoid over-provisioning)
Stop unused instances
Use Auto Scaling
Use:
Reserved Instances (up to 75% savings)
Spot Instances (up to 90% savings)
👉 Example:
If CPU usage is <20%, downgrade instance type
